1. Project Objective
The primary objective of this project is to design and implement an energy-efficient, hardware-driven motion-activated lighting system that operates without requiring microcontrollers or software programming.
•	Automated Human Presence Detection: To automatically activate an electric light source upon detecting human thermal movement within a 3 to 7-meter range.
•	Hardware-Only Switching Logic: To eliminate microcontrollers (such as Arduino or ESP) by using discrete analog components (BC547 NPN Transistor) for low-cost electronic switching.
•	Energy Conservation: To significantly reduce electrical power waste by ensuring lighting loads operate only when active movement is detected and shut off automatically after a set delay.
•	Practical Versatility: To develop a modular foundation that can be easily scaled to drive higher power AC loads via relay modules or trigger security alarms.

