6. Applications, Advantages & Limitations
Key Advantages:
•	Zero Microcontroller Cost: Highly economical solution requiring no programming or complex microchip hardware.
•	Energy Efficient: Power is consumed by the main load only when human presence is detected.
•	Instant Response: Transistor saturation switching provides immediate turn-ON capability.
•	Adjustable Timing & Range: Onboard PIR potentiometers allow tuning delay duration and distance.
Practical Applications:
•	Automatic Lighting: Staircases, corridors, washrooms, and garage entryways.
•	Intruder Alarm System: Circuit can drive a 9V buzzer or relay module instead of an LED.
•	Smart Home Automation: Automated night lamp switching to conserve household energy.
Circuit Limitations:
•	Line-of-Sight Restriction: PIR sensor cannot detect movement through solid walls or glass.
•	Thermal Sensitivity: High ambient outdoor temperatures (near 37°C) reduce detection accuracy.
•	Current Output Limit: BC547 transistor supports up to 100mA collector current; driving AC loads requires an additional relay module.
